  "comments": [
    {"at":0,"placement":"line","text":"Part of the developer's symbol table: 12-byte records of a 6-byte name, $a8 $00, the value and two bytes. A colon marks a local name."},
    {"at":0,"placement":"side","text":"Tail of a record with the value $81d5."},
    {"at":44,"placement":"side","text":"OPTION = $81f0, the routine that shows the player mode."},
    {"at":344,"placement":"side","text":"MASQUE = $842e. The values agree with the addresses of this build."},
    {"at":356,"placement":"side","text":"The last record breaks off after the name."},
    {"at":364,"placement":"line","text":"Name # of the buffer channel 5 that the disk check opens."},
    {"at":365,"placement":"line","text":"Drive command U1:5,0,18,18: reads track 18 sector 18 into channel 5."},
    {"at":377,"placement":"line","text":"Disk check that nothing calls. It reads track 18 sector 18 and expects drive error 23. Else it clears $7000-$70ff. Then it starts the game."},
    {"at":423,"placement":"side","text":"Sends the block read command on channel 15."},
    {"at":446,"placement":"side","text":"The first two characters of the drive status must be 23."},
    {"at":460,"placement":"side","text":"Reads the rest of the status message."},
    {"at":481,"placement":"side","text":"Error 23: starts the game."},
    {"at":484,"placement":"side","text":"Other status: fills $7000-$70ff with 0 32 times."},
    {"at":507,"placement":"line","text":"Bytes after the disk check that nothing uses."}
  ],
